# SHA-256 of every upstream file this package ships unmodified from
# geographiclib-c v2.2 (tag v2.2, commit
# 321c9a61359661fc2afa650dc888f5b1f5652443,
# https://github.com/geographiclib/geographiclib-c.git).
#
# 23 records. The set is the complete file list of the pinned upstream commit as
# it stands in this working tree, minus `.gitignore` (see "Deliberately absent"
# below). geographiclib-c is a small standalone project: the whole upstream tree
# is 24 files and 338,003 bytes, so a dependent receives upstream's project
# rather than a hand-picked subset of it. Nothing is dropped for size, and
# nothing is dropped for being unusable by this build: `doc/`, `tools/`,
# `proj-example/` and every `CMakeLists.txt` travel even though the Zig build
# compiles none of them, so the audit surface stays the whole upstream tree.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   .gitignore -- upstream's three lines (`*~`, `BUILD*/`, `distrib-C/`) are kept
#     verbatim and the Zig build cache entries are appended after them, so the
#     file is no longer byte-identical to upstream's. The pristine upstream
#     digest is recorded as a comment on its own line below rather than as a
#     checkable record, and the append is itemised in NOTICE.md.
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, zig/, tests.zig, smoke.zig, consumer/,
#   cross-test.profile.sh, .github/workflows/verify.yml, testdata/,
#   UPSTREAM.sha256, UPSTREAM.md, NOTICE.md, README.zig.md, README.md,
#   FORK-LICENSE.md, CHANGELOG.md, FORK-NOTES.md, package.nix, flake.nix,
#   devenv.nix, devenv.yaml and .envrc -- this fork's own files, listed in
#   NOTICE.md. flake.lock and devenv.lock are not in the tree either: they are
#   the driver's to create, and this record does not cover generated files.
#
# One record names a path that is not the upstream path. Upstream's README.md
# was preserved byte for byte as README.upstream.md when this fork's README.md
# took over the fork README, so the record reads README.upstream.md with the
# same digest it always had. The bytes are unchanged; only the name in the tree
# moved, and the name in a record has to move with the file. NOTICE.md and
# CHANGELOG.md entry 22 carry the relocation; README.upstream.md is upstream's
# standalone C README and not the C++ GeographicLib README.
#
# These are the bytes in this working tree, hashed with `sha256sum` on
# 2026-10-03 after the clone was checked out at the pinned commit. They are not a
# signature and not a Git object id: see UPSTREAM.md, "Integrity", for what they
# do and do not establish. No Git command was run to produce them; the working
# tree's identity as the pinned commit is stated in UPSTREAM.md from `.git/HEAD`
# and `.git/packed-refs`, which were read as files.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
#
# Pristine upstream `.gitignore`, 22 bytes, for the record only:
#   f030240ae4d14a041632c0b3f94fa9211f594cc7ad7b54d9a0e1a8dc33b93828  .gitignore
